                    comment Comment15 START <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd"><html><head><meta name="qrichtext" content="1" /><meta charset="utf-8" /><style type="text/css">p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }li.unchecked::marker { content: "\2610"; }li.checked::marker { content: "\2612"; }</style></head><body style=" font-family:'Sans'; font-size:12pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;"><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;"><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';">At the start of the simulation, </span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-weight:700;">the Signal Switch</span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';"> is configured to pass the </span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-weight:700;">F input (input 2)</span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';">, <br />which represents the initial RMS value of the active or reactive current.</span></p><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;"><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';">While the Signal Switch components are still passing the F inputs (inputs 2), <br />the </span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-weight:700;">Master Pulse is set to 1</span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';">, allowing the </span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-weight:700;">Sample and Hold components</span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';"> <br />to update and store the calculated active and reactive current values.</span></p><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;"><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';">After a short delay, Signal Switch components transition to the </span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-weight:700;">T inputs (inputs 1)</span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';">, <br />which correspond to the calculated active or reactive currents.</span></p><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;"><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI';">This approach improves the stability of the overall control logic during simulation startup.</span></p></body></html> ENDCOMMENT 
